%N A399491 The smallest integer m > n such that (n^2+1)*(m^2+1) is a perfect square.
%C A399491 a(n) <= 4*n^3+3*n.
%C A399491 a(n) < 4*n^3+3*n when n is in {7, 38, 41, 117, 268, 515, 682, 882, ...}.
%H A399491 Zhining Yang, <a href="/A399491/b399491.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..1000</a>
%t A399491 a[n_]:=Do[If[IntegerQ@Sqrt[(n^2+1) (m^2+1)],Return[m]],{m,n+1,Infinity}];Table[a[n],{n,40}]
%Y A399491 Cf. A002315, A173962, A271636.
